    {
      "id": "1-architectural-overview-design-philosophy",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "1. Architectural Overview & Design Philosophy"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Retiam features a dual 3D graphics pipeline:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            "**Explicit Polygonal Mesh Pipeline**: Classical vertex/index buffer rasterization and path tracing for standard primitives (`Box`, `Sphere`, `Cylinder`, `Torus`, `Model`, `Terrain3D`, `ParametricModel`).",
            "**Volumetric Signed Distance Field (SDF) Raymarching Pipeline**: Raymarched mathematical surfaces with exact smooth Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG), domain repetition, shelling, twisting, and continuous topological morphing."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "mermaid",
          "code": "flowchart TD\n  E[\"3D entity specification\"] --> M[\"Polygonal meshes<br/>ModelGeometry / VBO / IBO\"]\n  E --> S[\"Implicit SDF volumes<br/>SDFNode AST / WGSL\"]\n  M --> R[\"WebGPU rasterizer<br/>GBuffer / Shadow\"]\n  M --> T[\"WebGPU path tracer<br/>TLAS / BLAS / MIS\"]\n  S --> V[\"WebGPU raymarcher<br/>SDFVolume bounding box\"]\n  R --> C[\"FrameGraph composite pass\"]\n  T --> C\n  V --> C"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-3d-polygonal-primitives-catalogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "2. 3D Polygonal Primitives Catalogue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Located in [`src/engine/entities/primitives/3d/`](https://github.com/abhilasbiswas/Retiam/blob/main/src/engine/entities/primitives/3d):"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "Geometric Primitives"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "**`Box`**: Configurable width, height, depth with UV mapping and normal generation.",
            "**`Sphere`**: UV-sphere tessellated with configurable rings and segments.",
            "**`Cylinder` & `Cone`**: Cap tessellation and smooth cylindrical normals.",
            "**`Torus`**: Ring radius $R$ and tube radius $r$ parameterized over $(u, v) \\in [0, 2\\pi]^2$.",
            "**`Plane`**: Subdivided quadrilateral ground plane.",
            "**`Terrain3D`**: Heightmap-driven terrain generated from simplex/perlin noise or custom height evaluation functions."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "Parametric & Morphing Surfaces"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "**`ParametricModel`**: Generates complex 3D manifolds by evaluating continuous parametric functions:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "math",
          "tex": "(u, v) \\mapsto \\big(x(u, v), y(u, v), z(u, v)\\big)"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Includes automatic finite-difference normal calculation:"
        },
        {
          "type": "math",
          "tex": "\\vec{n} = \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{S}}{\\partial u} \\times \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{S}}{\\partial v}"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "**`MorphModel`**: Hardware-interpolated morphing between two distinct 3D topological meshes (`meshA` and `meshB`)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "Rich Media & Motion Tracers"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "**`RTImage` & `RTVideo`**: 3D textured quad elements capable of binding HTML5 video textures directly to GPU samplers via `texture_external`.",
            "**`RTHTML`**: 3D floating DOM elements projected into world coordinates.",
            "**`TracePath`**: Dynamically extruded ribbon mesh that continuously traces the trajectory of moving entities or particles over time."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3-volumetric-raymarching-sdfvolume-ts-src-engine-entities-primitives-3d-sdfvolume-ts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "3. Volumetric Raymarching ([SDFVolume.ts](../src/engine/entities/primitives/3d/SDFVolume.ts))"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Rather than raymarching across the entire screen, Retiam encapsulates implicit math surfaces inside **tightly-bounded oriented bounding boxes**:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "The rasterizer renders the outer faces of the bounding box.",
            "The fragment shader casts a ray starting from the box's entry point along the camera viewing direction:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "math",
          "tex": "\\vec{r}(t) = \\vec{p}_{\\text{entry}} + t \\cdot \\vec{d}_{\\text{ray}}"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Ray stepping uses sphere tracing:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "math",
          "tex": "t_{k+1} = t_k + d(\\vec{r}(t_k))"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "If $d < \\epsilon$, a surface hit is registered. If $t > t_{\\text{exit}}$, the ray exits the volume without hitting."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "Accurate Normal Estimation"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Surface normals are computed on the GPU via central differences:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "wgsl",
          "code": "fn calcNormal(p: vec3<f32>) -> vec3<f32> {\n    let e = vec2<f32>(0.001, -0.001);\n    return normalize(\n        e.xyy * map(p + e.xyy) +\n        e.yyx * map(p + e.yyx) +\n        e.yxy * map(p + e.yxy) +\n        e.xxx * map(p + e.xxx)\n    );\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4-constructive-solid-geometry-csg-ast-sdfnode-ts-src-engine-entities-sdf-sdfnode-ts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "4. Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) AST ([SDFNode.ts](../src/engine/entities/sdf/SDFNode.ts))"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Retiam provides a fluent TypeScript AST that compiles directly into optimized WGSL shader logic:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "typescript",
          "code": "// Construct a smooth union of a sphere and a rounded box with a hollowed center:\nconst sphere = new SDFSphere(1.2);\nconst box = new SDFBox([1.0, 1.0, 1.0]).round(0.1);\nconst csgTree = sphere.union(box, 0.2).subtract(new SDFCylinder(0.5, 2.0));\n\n// Instantiate the entity\nconst entity = new SDFEntity3D(csgTree);\nscene.add(entity);"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "CSG AST Hierarchy & WGSL Compilation"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "columns": [
            "Operation",
            "AST Node Class",
            "WGSL Function Output",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Union**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFUnion`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`opUnion(a, b)` or `opSmoothUnion(a, b, k)`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Combines shapes with optional polynomial smooth blend ($k$)."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Subtract**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFSubtract`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`opSubtraction(b, a)` or `opSmoothSubtraction(b, a, k)`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Carves shape $a$ out of shape $b$."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Intersect**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFIntersect`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`opIntersection(a, b)` or `opSmoothIntersection(a, b, k)`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Keeps only overlapping volume."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Translate**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFTranslate`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`map(p - offset)`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Moves the local sampling coordinate."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Rotate**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFRotate`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`map(R^T * p)`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Rotates the evaluation domain."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Scale**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFScale`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`map(p / s) * s`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Isotropically scales the distance field."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Repeat**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFRepeat`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`opRepeat(p, spacing)`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Infinitely tiles the geometry across space in $O(1)$ cost."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Mirror**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFMirror`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`map(abs(p))`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Reflects geometry across coordinate axes."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Twist**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFTwist`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`opTwist(p, k)`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Twists coordinate space around the vertical axis."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Shell**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFShell`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`abs(map(p)) - thickness`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Converts a solid volume into a hollow shell."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "cells": [
                {
                  "text": "**Morph**",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`SDFMorph`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "`mix(mapA(p), mapB(p), weight)`"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Dynamically transitions between two completely arbitrary topologies."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "text": "Bounding Box Propagation (getAABB())"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Every node in the AST calculates its exact Axis-Aligned Bounding Box:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Unions compute bounding box unions ($\\min(\\text{min}_A, \\text{min}_B)$, $\\max(\\text{max}_A, \\text{max}_B)$).",
            "Translations and rotations transform the bounding bounds.",
            "The parent [`SDFEntity3D`](https://github.com/abhilasbiswas/Retiam/blob/main/src/engine/entities/sdf/SDFEntity3D.ts) uses the root AABB to size the `SDFVolume`, ensuring zero raymarching overhead outside the shape bounds."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
